<http://data.silknow.org/object/d07d7cf4-ff8a-37c7-9247-c457e84531b8>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Scarf of silk and woollen gauze, Great Britain, ca. 1830-1850."@en , "Scarf of white gauze, silk warp and woollen weft. Into the open weave, at either end, are additional pattern wefts in scarlet, maronn and a mid-green wool. Squat pines are filled with large flowerheads. Between them are flower fillings in upward thrusting and downward trailing triangles, with one tiny sprig below the tip of each pine. Guard-stripes of a stiff floral meander in the same colours are flanked by bands of more closely woven white gauze with edges of blue silk. Above this is a cresting in scarlet, maroon and green.\n\nDown both sides of the scraf is a broad multiple stripe in silk, white flanked by narrow stripes of blue, green, black, white, scarlet and green. The fringe, knotted in at each end, is of white silk added at the sides to complement the colours of the broad stripe."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/161afe99-0cd0-319d-9aa7-c50013064536> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/1d99b0ff-7920-327d-b267-1257b700f288> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/adb85c82-c5f4-3fe5-a554-7f1416e84ffa> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Scarf of white gauze, silk warp and woollen weft. Into the open weave, at either end, are additional pattern wefts in scarlet, maronn and a mid-green wool. Squat pines are filled with large flowerheads. Between them are flower fillings in upward thrusting and downward trailing triangles, with one tiny sprig below the tip of each pine. Guard-stripes of a stiff floral meander in the same colours are flanked by bands of more closely woven white gauze with edges of blue silk. Above this is a cresting in scarlet, maroon and green.\n\nDown both sides of the scraf is a broad multiple stripe in silk, white flanked by narrow stripes of blue, green, black, white, scarlet and green. The fringe, knotted in at each end, is of white silk added at the sides to complement the colours of the broad stripe."@en , "Scarf of silk and woollen gauze, Great Britain, ca. 1830-1850."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/d07d7cf4-ff8a-37c7-9247-c457e84531b8/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/d07d7cf4-ff8a-37c7-9247-c457e84531b8/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/d07d7cf4-ff8a-37c7-9247-c457e84531b8/dimension/3> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/d07d7cf4-ff8a-37c7-9247-c457e84531b8/dimension/1> ;
